course: dictionary
lesson: 5791
title: A clever monkey called a macaque
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A macaque is a kind of monkey, and it is a noun, so you can have one macaque or many macaques. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it. «Macaques are clever, bold monkeys of Asia» tells you what they are, where they live and how they act.
explain: Clues can also tell you what a word does not mean. «Japanese macaques sit in hot springs in snowy winters to keep warm» tells you they are not cold-loving creatures that hide from snow. They are monkeys that stay warm in hot water when it is freezing outside.
explain: Some names are followed by extra words, like «rhesus macaque» or «Barbary macaque». These extra words name a particular kind of macaque. Read the whole phrase before you decide what it means.
fact: A macaque is a kind of monkey with a short tail or no tail.
fact: Most macaques live in Asia, and one kind, the Barbary macaque, lives in North Africa and also on Gibraltar.
fact: Japanese macaques are called snow monkeys because they bathe in hot springs in winter.
fact: Macaques are clever: they learn from each other, like the young female who taught her troop to wash sweet potatoes.
fact: In tourist areas, macaques may grab food, bags or phones, so it is unwise to feed them or touch them.
exercise: «Macaques are clever, bold monkeys of Asia.» What is a macaque? | A kind of fish | *A kind of monkey | A town in Thailand | A kind of tall tree
exercise: «Japanese macaques sit in hot springs in snowy winters to keep warm.» Why do they sit in hot springs? | Because the water is cold and fresh | *To keep warm in the snow | To catch fish | To hide from other monkeys
exercise: Which place is home to the Barbary macaques? | Japan | *Gibraltar | Thailand | China
test: «The Monkey King is a story hero, but rhesus macaques really live wild in China.» Are rhesus macaques real or only in stories? | Only in Japan, in hot springs | Pets that live in every home | *Real, and they live wild in China | Only in stories, like the Monkey King
test: Why is it unwise to feed macaques in tourist areas? | Because they are sleepy and might bite | Because they only eat leaves | Because they cannot see people | *Because they may grab food or bags
exam: «In Japan a young female macaque began washing sandy sweet potatoes in water.» What clever thing did she do? | *Washed her food in water | Climbed a mountain to find food | Built a nest of sticks | Sang a song to her troop
